S=[
('T201','Admit allocation through conditional SQL RETURNING','Conditional native UPDATE affects one quota row only when capacity remains; that receipt controls SQL allocation and KV document/index creation.', 'Native zero-row conditional DML could be mistaken for accepted allocation or a queued contender could observe partial cross-surface accounting.', ['Seed cap10/used0 and empty allocation table.', 'Left reserves7 with UPDATE RETURNING, pauses before document/index creation, then completes it.', 'Right attempts5 after queued admission and gets an ordinary empty receipt; no exception or injected failure.'], 'quota used7/cap10; only allocation a/7; KV count1, doc/a size7, index/a true. No b residue.', ['T001','T031','D214'], 'T001/T031 supply reused ordering controls; D214 unconditionally inserts two RETURNING rows. New credit is bounded conditional mutation receipt governing a compound allocation.', [ref(R,519,678,'Ordinary UPDATE/INSERT and application schema are allowed SQL actions.')], ['https://www.sqlite.org/lang_returning.html'], 'gatekeeper allocation/accounting'),
('T202','Deduplicate payloads with UPSERT reference accounting','Native UPSERT takes a first-insert then conflict-update path while preserving one BLOB and adding a second logical document.', 'UPSERT may replace the existing payload or return stale reference count, making physical versus logical byte charges diverge.', ['Create empty blob/link tables.', 'Left inserts content-123 [1,2,3] ref1, holds, then creates document a.', 'Right UPSERT increments refs to2 and creates document b using the same content row.'], 'one BLOB [1,2,3] refs2; links a,b to content-123; documents2, logical6, physical3.', ['T001','T019','D212','D214'], 'No baseline tests native UPSERT conflict-update plus shared payload reference accounting. BLOB conversion and transaction queue alone earn no credit.', [], ['https://www.sqlite.org/lang_upsert.html'], 'gatekeeper shared payload accounting'),
('T203','Maintain folder totals through SQL triggers','Native INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE trigger bodies maintain both sides of a collection move while explicit KV indexes follow the same transaction.', 'The update trigger may leave one folder charged, or later deletion could use stale pre-move totals.', ['Seed a/x/3 and b/x/4 through insertion trigger.', 'Left moves a to y and resizes to5, holds before KV rekey.', 'Right observes x1/4,y1/5 then deletes b through deletion trigger.'], 'folders x count0/bytes0, y count1/bytes5; SQL only a/y/5; KV only y/a=5.', ['T008','D218'], 'D218 tests ingest parser boundaries and trigger row-count metadata. Here ordinary exec triggers maintain old/new relational aggregates across queued requests; sql.ingest is not used.', [ref(R,618,632,'Ordinary application trigger definitions are allowed by authorizer.')], ['https://www.sqlite.org/lang_createtrigger.html'], 'typed-storage indexed collection counts'),
('T204','Cascade renamed document ownership into chunks','Native foreign keys cascade primary-key rename and later parent deletion into composite-key chunk rows; an unrelated document survives.', 'Chunk ownership may stay at the old document key or become orphaned after the renamed parent is deleted.', ['Enable foreign_keys outside transactions; seed a3 with two chunks and keep2 with one.', 'Left renames a to renamed, holds, then rekeys KV.', 'Right verifies renamed child rows and deletes renamed parent.'], 'only parent keep/2 and chunk keep/0/[8,9]; foreign_key_check empty; KV bytes2,count1,doc/keep2.', ['T003','T027','D210'], 'Existing deletion tests cover KV counts/rollback, not native ON UPDATE and ON DELETE cascade propagation through relational ownership.', [ref(R,519,540,'foreign_keys and foreign_key_check are public allowlisted pragmas.')], ['https://www.sqlite.org/foreignkeys.html'], 'gatekeeper file/chunk ownership'),
('T205','Commit deferred head references with nested revisions','A DEFERRABLE INITIALLY DEFERRED cyclic document/head relationship is temporarily unresolved inside a valid transaction and completed by an awaited successful child savepoint.', 'An implementation may enforce the deferred relationship prematurely at child/outer boundaries or expose the unresolved head to the queued peer.', ['Create cyclic docs/head and versions/doc foreign keys, seed revision1 in a valid transaction.', 'Left changes head to2, holds before version2 exists, then inserts version2 in awaited child transaction.', 'Right observes complete head2 before similarly committing head3/version3.'], 'no foreign-key violations; versions1/2bytes,2/4bytes,3/2bytes; SQL head3 and KV head revision3/bytes2.', ['T004','T008','T009'], 'Nested commit ownership is reused, not counted. New mechanism is valid deferred cyclic relational integrity across successful nested savepoints and cross-surface head state. No failing commit is attempted.', [ref(J,1898,1909,'Awaited transaction-view child uses native nested savepoint.'),ref(R,519,540,'Foreign-key enforcement may be explicitly enabled before transaction entry.')], ['https://www.sqlite.org/foreignkeys.html#fk_deferred'], 'typed-storage document revision integrity'),
('T206','Select active document through a partial unique index','A partial UNIQUE index releases an archived slug and an UPSERT conflict target WHERE live=1 selects only the replacement active row.', 'A conflict target could update an archived same-slug row or allocate a third live identity, disconnecting the current KV index.', ['Seed active id1/report/2 and archived id99/report/7.', 'Left archives1 and creates active2/report/4, holds, then points KV slug to2.', 'Right attempts id3/report/6 with partial-index UPSERT; the actual result is id2/6.'], 'archived1/2 and99/7 unchanged; active2/6 only; active count1/bytes6; KV slug/report2.', ['D214','T024','T001'], 'Distinct from schema recompilation T024 and unconditional RETURNING D214. Native partial-index conflict selection preserves historical identities; it is not another quota UPDATE.', [ref(R,598,615,'Application index definitions are permitted.')], ['https://www.sqlite.org/partialindex.html','https://www.sqlite.org/lang_upsert.html'], 'typed-storage live versus archived indexes'),
('T207','Extract bounded KV partitions into SQL accounting','A finite prefix list selects a page whose rows move into SQL before bulk deletion and remaining-byte accounting; the next queued extraction must select the next disjoint page.', 'A page could be extracted twice or lose its remaining-byte update across the KV/SQL atomic boundary.', ['Seed pending/a1,b2,c3,d4,e5 and adjacent-prefix decoy99.', 'Left selects a,b, inserts archive rows, holds before deleting selected keys, then writes remaining12.', 'Right selects c,d, archives and deletes them, then writes remaining5.'], 'archive a1,b2,c3,d4 count4/bytes10; only pending/e5, adjacent decoy99 and remaining5 stay in KV.', ['D207','D210','T027','T028'], 'Those cases establish individual list bounds, deletion counts, rollback and microtask ordering. This candidate asserts a disjoint two-request destructive partition transfer with a fixed cross-store conservation oracle; reviewer may withhold credit if judged redundant.', [ref(J,1653,1668,'Public list and delete-many paths.'),ref(R,3606,3731,'Distinct existing-key deletion and bounded prefix scan implementation.')], ['https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/api/sqlite-storage-api/#list'], 'typed-storage bounded indexed collection scans'),
('T208','Rebuild bounded recursive ancestry accounting','Native recursive CTEs derive materialized ancestry after a subtree move; a queued insert uses the new graph and all ancestor rollups must agree.', 'Descendant membership can be omitted or counted twice when a stored parent graph and derived index diverge.', ['Seed four acyclic directories and three documents; derive ancestry.', 'Left moves directory1 beneath3 and rebuilds ancestry through a depth-capped recursive CTE, then holds.', 'Right checks subtree3=15 and adds d2bytes in directory2 using the new ancestry.'], 'ancestor0 count4/17bytes; ancestor1 count3/10; ancestor2 count2/5; ancestor3 count4/17; graph 1->3->0,2->1; KV total17,parent/1=3.', ['T030'], 'T030 runs an unrelated fixed 64x64 arithmetic query. This is a native recursive traversal feeding INSERT with relational membership and aggregate consistency, never a scalability or liveness benchmark.', [], ['https://www.sqlite.org/lang_with.html'], 'typed-storage hierarchical collection indexes'),
('T209','Prune revision partitions with window-ranked retention','Native row_number partitioning selects obsolete unpinned versions for DELETE RETURNING while preserving each document current pointer and byte total.', 'Pruning can cross document partitions, delete pinned history or mischarge deleted payloads.', ['Seed a revisions1(pinned),2,3 and independent b1.', 'Left inserts a4, prunes a2 by rank, holds, then updates head/byte counters.', 'Right inserts a5 and prunes a3 through the same fixed retention rule.'], 'versions a1/1 pinned,a4/4,a5/5,b1/7; total17; heads a5,b1. Exactly a2 then a3 deleted.', ['D214','T027'], 'New native window-function partitioning plus conditional row deletion, distinct from unconditional INSERT RETURNING and restored KV rollback. Repeated left/right actions form one case, not two credits.', [], ['https://www.sqlite.org/windowfunctions.html','https://www.sqlite.org/lang_returning.html'], 'typed-storage revision retention and accounting'),
('T210','Merge overlapping writes across chunk boundaries','Finite byte-range read/modify/write spans two native BLOB rows; the later request overwrites only its overlap and leaves allocation/size unchanged.', 'Chunk slice merging can discard preserved prefixes/suffixes or charge rewritten bytes as new allocation.', ['Seed two four-byte chunks with0..7.', 'Left writes offset2 [9,8,7] across boundary and holds.', 'Right reads the full first result then writes offset3 [6,5] across the same boundary.'], 'file bytes [0,1,9,6,5,5,6,7]; offsets0,4 lengths4,4; size8,chunks2,stored8.', ['T019','D201','D212'], 'Typed bind conversion is a reused prerequisite. New oracle is an exact multi-row overlapping range merge with preserved bytes and zero-growth accounting, not alias/snapshot ownership.', [ref(O,585,623,'Native bind/result conversion preserves bounded BLOB views.'),ref(R,3805,3860,'Native typed byte binding.')], ['https://www.sqlite.org/datatype3.html'], 'gatekeeper chunk mutation'),
('T211','Detect sparse extent gaps with native boundary windows','Native LAG of predecessor end offsets detects the exact hole between disjoint BLOB extents; queued gap-fill removes that gap while changing physical bytes without changing logical EOF.', 'Accounting can charge zero-fill as stored data or lose existing extents when filling the gap.', ['Seed offset0 bytes[1,2].', 'Left inserts offset8 [9,10], updates metadata size10/stored4, and holds.', 'Right native LAG boundary query returns gap[2,8], checks stored-byte metadata, then inserts offset2 [3..8].'], 'Native gap rows initially [{gap_start:2,gap_end:8}], then empty; extents offsets0/2bytes,2/6bytes,8/2bytes; file [1..10]; size10/chunks3/stored10, with intermediate size10/stored4.', ['D212','T019','T210'], 'T210 overwrites existing fixed chunks. This native LAG predecessor-boundary query discovers an actual extent gap and proves its removal after fill; fixture zero-fill earns no independent credit. T209 ranks whole revision rows for retention, whereas this case computes interval adjacency from BLOB lengths and offsets.', [ref(O,585,623,'Exact BLOB byte conversion.')], ['https://www.sqlite.org/lang_corefunc.html','https://www.sqlite.org/windowfunctions.html'], 'gatekeeper sparse allocation accounting'),
('T212','Trim native BLOB ranges before boundary append','Native DELETE removes tail extents and substr clips a crossing BLOB; a queued append fills that partial chunk then creates a new one.', 'Truncation may retain discarded suffix bytes, release the wrong charge or cause later append to resurrect the old tail.', ['Seed ten bytes in chunks of4,4,2.', 'Left truncates to6 using DELETE+substr, updates metadata, and holds.', 'Right observes exact six-byte prefix and appends [11,12,13].'], 'file [1,2,3,4,5,6,11,12,13]; chunks0/4,4/4,8/1; size9,chunks3,stored9. Intermediate size6/stored6.', ['D210','D212','T210','T211'], 'Distinct native deletion plus BLOB truncation path, then partial terminal reuse; neither existing overwrite nor sparse gap-fill removes physical data or clips native BLOBs.', [ref(R,1616,1675,'Native result rows preserve BLOBs rather than text coercing them.')], ['https://www.sqlite.org/lang_corefunc.html#substr'], 'gatekeeper file shrink and append accounting'),
('T213','Publish complete chunk manifest with conserved charge','A native aggregate HAVING predicate validates contiguous fixed chunks before materializing a manifest and transferring reserved bytes into live bytes.', 'Publication can count only byte sum while overlooking a missing/overlapping chunk, or charge both staged and committed data.', ['Seed two of three valid chunks with reserved6/live0.', 'Left inserts the final chunk then holds before marking staged6.', 'Right validates sequence, offsets, lengths and aggregate6, creates manifest, transfers charge and removes staging marker.'], 'manifest f/chunks3/bytes6; quota reserved0/live6; chunks offsets0,2,4 with payload1..6; only KV complete file descriptor remains.', ['T001','D206','T201'], 'No new generic queue credit. Unlike conditional quota UPDATE, this admission is a multi-row relational completeness reduction with manifest creation and a two-bucket charge transfer.', [], ['https://www.sqlite.org/lang_select.html'], 'gatekeeper allocation/chunk/finalization accounting'),
('T214','Index generated UTF-8 payload byte lengths','Stored generated byte length and virtual character length recompute on text mutation; an index on generated bytes must agree with document accounting.', 'Generated index maintenance or text/BLOB conversion could confuse UTF-8 bytes with codepoints or JS UTF-16 units.', ['Seed A and zz with total3 bytes.', 'Left replaces A with é🦉, obtains n6/chars2, holds, then sets total8.', 'Right reads generated-byte index then replaces zz with λ, preserving two-byte charge.'], 'a bodyé🦉 n6/chars2; b bodyλ n2/chars1; indexed n>=6 selects onlya; sum n8 and KV bytes8.', ['D212','T024'], 'Basic text conversion and schema recompilation are reused. New mechanism is stored/virtual generated recomputation and native generated-column index maintenance during ordinary rewrites.', [ref(R,598,615,'Application index creation allowed.'),ref(R,1616,1675,'SQLite native text and integer results.')], ['https://www.sqlite.org/gencol.html','https://www.sqlite.org/lang_corefunc.html'], 'typed-storage indexed payload byte accounting'),
('T215','Reconcile FTS postings with document byte totals','Native FTS5 virtual-table UPDATE removes old token postings and DELETE removes another document while KV documents and counts track the same transactions.', 'Search postings can outlive document edits/deletion or virtual-table row content can diverge from document/count/byte state.', ['Seed a red blue and b red orange with total18.', 'Left updates a to green blue, holds, then writes KV and total20.', 'Right searches red and sees onlyb, deletes b, and writes count1/bytes10.'], 'MATCH red empty; MATCH green AND blue yields only a/green blue; FTS count1/bytes10; KV only doc/a plus matching totals.', ['D218','T024'], 'No FTS5 posting mutation case exists in T001–T032 or D201–D220. Ordinary virtual-table index maintenance is a separate native path from SQL triggers or cached schema statements.', [ref(R,578,588,'FTS5 virtual table module is explicitly allowlisted; ordinary extension loading is not used.')], ['https://www.sqlite.org/fts5.html'], 'synthetic OS document search/index consistency'),
]
